{"nodes": [{"id": "claude_skills_performance_references_gpu_metal", "label": "GPU (Metal / MSL) practices for MetalRenderer", "file_type": "document", "source_file": ".claude/skills/performance/references/gpu-metal.md", "source_location": "L1", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "claude_skills_performance_references_gpu_metal_apple_silicon_gpu", "label": "Apple-silicon GPU traits (unified memory, 32-wide simdgroups, no RT hardware on M1/M2)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": ".claude/skills/performance/references/gpu-metal.md", "source_location": "L3", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "On M1/M2 Metal's intersector is software, so the project's own BVH (CUSTOM_RT) can beat it; re-check on M3 and later with METALRENDERER_BENCH=rt."}, {"id": "claude_skills_performance_references_gpu_metal_frame_submission", "label": "Frame structure and submission (one command buffer per frame, overlap is real performance)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": ".claude/skills/performance/references/gpu-metal.md", "source_location": "L12", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Split passes and fenced encoders serialize the frame and add overhead, so they are for timing only and never ship on the normal path."}, {"id": "claude_skills_performance_references_gpu_metal_per_slot_buffers", "label": "Per-slot ring buffers for CPU writes (slot = frameIndex % 3)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": ".claude/skills/performance/references/gpu-metal.md", "source_location": "L20", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Writing a buffer the GPU may still be reading is a race, not just a slowdown."}, {"id": "claude_skills_performance_references_gpu_metal_memory_bandwidth", "label": "Memory bandwidth: the default suspect for screen-space passes", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": ".claude/skills/performance/references/gpu-metal.md", "source_location": "L27", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Temporal, a-trous, composite, fog and upscaler passes read and write several full-screen textures per pixel and do little math, so shrink formats (rgba16Float norm), read only needed channels, fuse passes and lower rates."}, {"id": "claude_skills_performance_references_gpu_metal_occupancy_registers", "label": "Occupancy and registers: the default suspect for big kernels", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": ".claude/skills/performance/references/gpu-metal.md", "source_location": "L53", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "When registers run out fewer threads run at once and memory latency stops being hidden. Dynamically indexed arrays inside loops over many items become stack traffic; vector lanes with select and groupMask measured -8% to -14% in manyLightsKernel and -12% in the composite."}, {"id": "claude_skills_performance_references_gpu_metal_compile_out_features", "label": "Compile out what's off (LIGHT_SPEC function constant, CUSTOM_RT and RT_STATS macros)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": ".claude/skills/performance/references/gpu-metal.md", "source_location": "L68", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A runtime if on a uniform is cheap for divergence but still reserves registers for both paths."}, {"id": "claude_skills_performance_references_gpu_metal_threadgroup_size_tuning", "label": "Threadgroup size tuning (Renderer.threadgroupSizes, METALRENDERER_TG)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": ".claude/skills/performance/references/gpu-metal.md", "source_location": "L73", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Defaults are 8x8, trace 16x8 (+2%) and atrous 16x16 (+5%); keep winners only if they hold across alternating runs."}, {"id": "claude_skills_performance_references_gpu_metal_divergence_access_patterns", "label": "Divergence and memory access patterns (uniform trip counts, 2D tiles)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": ".claude/skills/performance/references/gpu-metal.md", "source_location": "L79", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A simdgroup runs as slowly as its slowest lane."}, {"id": "claude_skills_performance_references_gpu_metal_one_fetch_per_decision", "label": "Lay data out for one fetch per decision (64-byte two-child BVH node, TLAS instance-mask OR)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": ".claude/skills/performance/references/gpu-metal.md", "source_location": "L84", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "One load tests both children; the TLAS hi.w carries an OR of instance masks so rays skip whole subtrees."}, {"id": "claude_skills_performance_references_gpu_metal_reductions_atomics", "label": "Reductions, atomics and threadgroup memory (relaxed atomics, simdgroup then threadgroup then global)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": ".claude/skills/performance/references/gpu-metal.md", "source_location": "L92", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "claude_skills_performance_references_gpu_metal_simdgroup_intrinsics", "label": "Simdgroup intrinsics (simd_sum, simd_ballot, quad_*): unused optimization opportunity", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": ".claude/skills/performance/references/gpu-metal.md", "source_location": "L96", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "They would replace threadgroup-memory round-trips, barriers and one-global-atomic-per-thread accumulations; only worth it when the pass shows up in timings."}, {"id": "claude_skills_performance_references_gpu_metal_threadgroup_tiles", "label": "Threadgroup tiles with an apron for neighbourhood filters", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": ".claude/skills/performance/references/gpu-metal.md", "source_location": "L105", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Use half in tiles, few barriers, and stay well below 32 KB per group so several groups stay resident per core."}, {"id": "claude_skills_performance_references_gpu_metal_math_practices", "label": "Shader math practices (CPU-precomputed constants, no integer division, select/mix/fma, fast math)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": ".claude/skills/performance/references/gpu-metal.md", "source_location": "L112", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Fast math is Metal's default; the closed-form area lights and sky integrals are checked by lightcheck and skycheck, to be re-run after touching their math."}, {"id": "claude_skills_performance_references_gpu_metal_acceleration_structures", "label": "Acceleration structures and ray tracing practices (static once, LBVH per frame, TLAS refit cadence)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": ".claude/skills/performance/references/gpu-metal.md", "source_location": "L122", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Ray count is the main budget on M1/M2; keep virtual-geometry cut changes rare because every rebuild costs CPU and memory churn."}, {"id": "claude_skills_performance_references_gpu_metal_pipelines_resources", "label": "Pipelines and resources (background compile of the whole set, on-disk pipeline cache, storage modes)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": ".claude/skills/performance/references/gpu-metal.md", "source_location": "L133", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Compile off the frame path and off the main thread so frames keep flowing and a failed reload keeps the old pipelines; warm builds of all 47 pipelines take 2-6 ms, cold source compile 1.9 s."}, {"id": "claude_skills_performance_references_gpu_metal_gpu_tools", "label": "GPU tools (Debug window, Xcode GPU frame capture, Instruments Metal System Trace)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": ".claude/skills/performance/references/gpu-metal.md", "source_location": "L150", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Frame capture is the tool for why, after the benchmark has said where."}], "edges": [{"source": "claude_skills_performance_references_gpu_metal", "target": "claude_skills_performance_references_gpu_metal_apple_silicon_gpu", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": ".claude/skills/performance/references/gpu-metal.md", "source_location": "L3", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "claude_skills_performance_references_gpu_metal", "target": "claude_skills_performance_references_gpu_metal_frame_submission", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": ".claude/skills/performance/references/gpu-metal.md", "source_location": "L12", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "claude_skills_performance_references_gpu_metal", "target": "claude_skills_performance_references_gpu_metal_memory_bandwidth", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": ".claude/skills/performance/references/gpu-metal.md", "source_location": "L27", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "claude_skills_performance_references_gpu_metal", "target": "claude_skills_performance_references_gpu_metal_occupancy_registers", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": ".claude/skills/performance/references/gpu-metal.md", "source_location": "L53", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "claude_skills_performance_references_gpu_metal", "target": "claude_skills_performance_references_gpu_metal_divergence_access_patterns", "relation": "r